        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Both brands build professional-grade cordless tools that will last a homeowner ten years and a tradesperson years of daily work. Milwaukee comes out ahead on specialty-tool breadth, the compact M12 lineup and a longer standard warranty. DeWalt comes out ahead on where you can buy it, FLEXVOLT high-power saws, frequent bundle deals and its satisfaction guarantee.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Choose the platform whose next five tools fit your work, then stick with it; that one decision saves more money and hassle than any spec-sheet shootout. If your needs are light, a budget platform may be the smarter purchase. Whichever way you go, back the cordless kit with good hand tools and a calibrated torque wrench for the jobs that call for precision.
          </p>
